<p>As humans, we border on an <strong>OBSESSION of control.</strong></p>
<p>We are control freaks - we want everything the way we want it. If we cannot have it that way, we will try to force the universe’s hand</p>
<p>Let’s do a thought experiment and see what we can <strong>ACTUALLY control in this life.</strong></p>
<h3><strong>1. How much you put yourself out into the world</strong><a href="#1-how-much-you-put-yourself-out-into-the-world">#</a></h3>
<p>You cannot control your first impression or what others think of you. You can only put yourself in front of more people. Eventually, you will find those people that <strong>love and value you</strong> if you do it enough.</p>
<h3><strong>2. Your mindset</strong><a href="#2-your-mindset">#</a></h3>
<p>Contrary to popular belief, your mind is the <strong>MOST CONTROLLABLE aspect of your existence</strong>.</p>
<p>You can decide right here and now to see things positively. You can create your outlook on this world and use that to shape your entire life. You can <strong>DECIDE to be happy, grateful, and to live in the here and now</strong>.  Nothing makes be more angry than when people say they cannot control their mindset.</p>
<p><strong>They simply haven’t tried.</strong></p>
<h3><strong>3. Your patience</strong><a href="#3-your-patience">#</a></h3>
<p>You can decide to be <strong>patient</strong>. You can decide to be <strong>calm</strong>.</p>
<p>Going through life with a hair trigger temper is <strong>fucking lame.</strong></p>
<h3><strong>4. Your physicality</strong><a href="#4-your-physicality">#</a></h3>
<p>I know first hand that you could break your back and be wheelchair bound. That’s not what I mean.</p>
<p>What I mean by this is that you can <strong>choose to move as a human being should</strong>. I’ve been in unbearable pain - <strong>movement is the only thing that consistently alleviates this pain</strong>.</p>
<p>Unless you are completely incapacitated and paralyzed (I was from the waist down) you do not have an excuse.</p>
<p><strong>The people that will criticise me on this one have no ground to stand on.</strong></p>
<h3><strong>5. The way you treat others</strong><a href="#5-the-way-you-treat-others">#</a></h3>
<p>Even if someone is completely rude to you, you can decide to treat them better than they treat you.</p>
<p>If someone is a complete asshole to you, consider the source.</p>
<p><strong>It may not even be YOU they are mad at.</strong></p>
<h3><strong>6. <a href="https://joshblais.com/blog/Show-up-early">Being on time</a></strong><a href="#6-being-on-time">#</a></h3>
<p>Yeah, traffic, blah blah. You can choose to leave 5 minutes early.</p>
<p><strong>Nothing shows more disrespect than being chronically late. Nothing shows more respect than being early for your engagements.</strong></p>
<h3><strong>7. How you listen</strong><a href="#7-how-you-listen">#</a></h3>
<p>You can control <strong>shutting the fuck up for a few minutes.</strong></p>
<h3><strong>8. How you spend your time</strong><a href="#8-how-you-spend-your-time">#</a></h3>
<p>You get <strong>24 hours in a day</strong>, the same as anyone else.</p>
<p>You can <em>create or you can consume</em>.</p>
<p>You can decide to watch Lameflix and jerk off.</p>
<p>Or you could be writing, reading, building, seeking. <strong>The choice is up to you</strong>.</p>
<h3><strong>9. The people you surround yourself with</strong><a href="#9-the-people-you-surround-yourself-with">#</a></h3>
<p>If the people around you are not making you better, or you feel that you are on a different wavelength <strong>STOP HANGING OUT WITH THEM</strong>.</p>
<p>Humans are social creatures, and we rise to the occasion, as well as fall to the lowest common denominator.</p>
<p>There are losers and winners in life.</p>
<p>Surround yourself with those that <strong>are winners</strong> or are <strong>on their path to winning</strong>.</p>
<p>Seek <strong>actual connection</strong>.</p>
<p>Do not seek to gain from others without giving.</p>
<p><strong>Look for depth of character.  Everything else is a waste of time.</strong></p>
<h3><strong>10. Your inputs</strong><a href="#10-your-inputs">#</a></h3>
<p>In addition to your mindset and outlook on life, you can decide what <em>you focus on, what you are allowing into your mind</em>.</p>
<p>You can control what you <strong>read, what you watch, what you listen to</strong>.</p>
<p>You can move conversation away from the banal and into whatever depth suits you.</p>
<p><strong>Control what you can control</strong></p>
<p>As always, God bless, and until next time.</p>
